{
  "design_rationale": "First-order-plus-delay heater: y_ss=y_amb+K*u with y_amb~0.15 from E2 settled 0.155 and K~1.0 from E4 settled 0.409 at u=0.25 (0.254/0.25=1.02). E1 0.5->0.52 after 200s still rising and E5 0.25->0.4 rising 0.41->0.53 in 170s extrapolate to 0.58-0.73, consistent with K~1.0-1.1, tau~150-200s, delay 10-25s. So hold for 0.5 is (0.5-0.15)/1.03~0.34. Use feedforward 0.34 plus PI for residual. Kp=0.65 gives P~0.23 for full 0.35 error -> u~0.57, heating ~0.0034/s, no saturation. Ki=0.008 (Ti~81s) trims offset without aggressive windup. Integrate only when |e|<0.15 so initial 0.35 error does not wind up integrator (would add ~0.13 overshoot otherwise). Integral +-0.25 leaves >2x authority over max FF error ~0.11. Filter Tf=15s vs tau 170s smooths 0.02-0.04 noise with negligible lag. U_MAX=0.65 plus yf>0.75/0.80 backstop guarantees steady y<0.82 nominal and forced cooling before 0.85/0.9 even if K=1.2. Rate limit 0.08/s smooths noise chatter.",
  "machine_card": "Heater: more power = hotter. Gain K~1.0-1.1 normalized y per unit u. Ambient (u=0) drains to 0.12-0.16 (~0.155). u=0.25 holds ~0.41 settled (E4 460s). u=0.5 after 200s at 0.52 still rising toward ~0.65-0.73; u=0.4 after 170s at 0.53 rising toward ~0.59. Lag: time constant ~150-200s, small pure delay ~10-25s. No dead zone (<0.1): 0.25 heats clearly. Self-draining: yes, falls to ambient when u=0 over ~400s. Noise: 0.02-0.04 peak, similar to band half-width 0.025, needs filtering. Hold for y=0.5 needs u~0.32-0.38 center ~0.34. Speed: worst 0.006/s per unit u, typical 0.002-0.0035/s near target. Stay below 0.65 sustained to stay below soft limit 0.85.",
  "operator_note": "Keeps temperature at 0.5 automatically. Starts near 0.57 power when cold then settles near 0.34 power. Filtered and rate-limited so heater moves smoothly. Has built-in overheat cutback above 0.75. No action needed.",
  "predicted_behavior": "From cold 0.15: u~0.57 initially, rise ~0.003/s, enter 0.475-0.525 in ~120-170s, settle within band by ~200-250s with overshoot <0.02 (typically <0.01) because integrator is frozen until within 0.15. From hot 0.55: cool with u~0.25-0.30 down into band in ~60-100s. Steady: y=0.50+-0.015 filtered, u~0.32-0.38 mean ~0.34, small +-0.015 dither from noise. Energy ~0.12 per sec (0.34^2). Never near 0.85/0.9 in normal tracking.",
  "self_test_expectations": [
    "control({}, {}) does not raise and returns finite u in [0,1] with yf init",
    "with y=0.15 target=0.5 first u is 0.50-0.65 (FF+P, not saturated, not zero)",
    "with y=0.5 target=0.5 after settling u is 0.25-0.45 near 0.34",
    "with yf>0.80 output is 0.0 regardless of integrator",
    "with yf>0.75 output capped <=0.10",
    "successive calls with dt=1 change u by <=0.09 (rate limit)",
    "100 steps at constant y=0.5 target=0.5 keeps u in [0,0.65] and integ in [-0.25,0.25]",
    "handles dt=0.2 and dt=2.0, NaN y, NaN dt without exception or NaN/inf or out-of-range"
  ],
  "source_code": "import math

def _clamp(v, lo, hi):
    if v < lo:
        return lo
    if v > hi:
        return hi
    return v

def control(obs, state):
    Y_AMB = 0.15
    K_EST = 1.03
    KP = 0.65
    KI = 0.008
    TF = 15.0
    I_MIN = -0.25
    I_MAX = 0.25
    U_MIN = 0.0
    U_MAX = 0.65
    INT_BAND = 0.15
    try:
        if isinstance(obs, dict):
            y_in = obs.get("y", 0.5)
            t_in = obs.get("target", 0.5)
            dt_in = obs.get("dt", 1.0)
        else:
            y_in = 0.5
            t_in = 0.5
            dt_in = 1.0
        y = float(y_in)
        target = float(t_in)
        dt = float(dt_in)
    except Exception:
        y = 0.5
        target = 0.5
        dt = 1.0
    if not math.isfinite(y):
        y = 0.5
    if not math.isfinite(target):
        target = 0.5
    if not math.isfinite(dt) or dt <= 0.0:
        dt = 1.0
    if dt < 0.05:
        dt = 0.05
    if dt > 5.0:
        dt = 5.0
    if target < 0.0:
        target = 0.0
    if target > 1.0:
        target = 1.0
    if y < 0.0:
        y = 0.0
    if y > 1.0:
        y = 1.0
    if not isinstance(state, dict):
        state = {}
    try:
        yf_prev = float(state.get("yf", y))
    except Exception:
        yf_prev = y
    try:
        integ_prev = float(state.get("integ", 0.0))
    except Exception:
        integ_prev = 0.0
    try:
        u_prev = float(state.get("u_prev", -1.0))
    except Exception:
        u_prev = -1.0
    if not math.isfinite(yf_prev):
        yf_prev = y
    if not math.isfinite(integ_prev):
        integ_prev = 0.0
    if not math.isfinite(u_prev):
        u_prev = -1.0
    yf_prev = _clamp(yf_prev, 0.0, 1.0)
    integ_prev = _clamp(integ_prev, I_MIN, I_MAX)
    alpha = dt / (TF + dt)
    if alpha < 0.0:
        alpha = 0.0
    if alpha > 1.0:
        alpha = 1.0
    yf = yf_prev + alpha * (y - yf_prev)
    if not math.isfinite(yf):
        yf = yf_prev
    yf = _clamp(yf, 0.0, 1.0)
    u_ff = (target - Y_AMB) / K_EST
    u_ff = _clamp(u_ff, U_MIN, U_MAX)
    e = target - yf
    p = KP * e
    integ = integ_prev
    if abs(e) < INT_BAND:
        cand = integ_prev + KI * e * dt
        cand = _clamp(cand, I_MIN, I_MAX)
        u_cand = u_ff + p + cand
        if u_cand > U_MAX and e > 0.0:
            integ = integ_prev
        elif u_cand < U_MIN and e < 0.0:
            integ = integ_prev
        else:
            integ = cand
    else:
        integ = integ_prev
    u_des = u_ff + p + integ
    u_des = _clamp(u_des, U_MIN, U_MAX)
    if yf > 0.80:
        u_des = U_MIN
        if integ > 0.0:
            integ = integ - 0.02 * dt
            if integ < I_MIN:
                integ = I_MIN
            if integ > I_MAX:
                integ = I_MAX
    elif yf > 0.75:
        if u_des > 0.10:
            u_des = 0.10
    if u_prev < -0.5:
        u_out = u_des
    else:
        up = _clamp(u_prev, U_MIN, U_MAX)
        max_du = 0.08 * dt
        if max_du < 0.005:
            max_du = 0.005
        if max_du > 0.30:
            max_du = 0.30
        du = u_des - up
        if du > max_du:
            du = max_du
        elif du < -max_du:
            du = -max_du
        u_out = up + du
    u_out = _clamp(u_out, U_MIN, U_MAX)
    if not math.isfinite(u_out):
        u_out = u_ff
    if u_out < 0.0:
        u_out = 0.0
    if u_out > 1.0:
        u_out = 1.0
    new_state = {"yf": float(yf), "integ": float(integ), "u_prev": float(u_out)}
    return (float(u_out), new_state)
"
}

{
 "change_summary": "Fixed high-side overshoot and slow low-side trim: lowered fixed feedforward from 0.340 (0.15/1.03) to ~0.318 (0.14/1.10), added slow online u* adaptation (KA=0.005) + stronger gated integral (KI 0.008->0.018, band 0.15->0.25, limits +-0.25->+-0.30), added filtered derivative-on-measurement braking (Kd=28, D+-0.12) with faster feedback filter (TF 15->8s) and slow reference filter (35s), raised U_MAX 0.65->0.68 for weaker-actuator headroom, kept safety cuts and rate limit. Targets the measured 0.04 hold-power overestimate and missing momentum braking.",
 "design_rationale": "Nominal plant is first-order tau~150-180s K~1.0-1.2 amb~0.12-0.15, hold u*~0.30 for y=0.5. v1 ff=0.34 is ~0.04 high, P alone cannot brake stored-heat momentum, and KI=0.008 inside |e|<0.15 needs >500s to learn -0.04, so y stays 0.53-0.57 for ~200s then sags to ~0.49. Fix: (a) start ff near observed 0.30 to remove bias on both nominal and changed plants, (b) slow ff-adaptation learns any new u* from y_slow error without windup, (c) larger gated integral trims residual in ~100-150s with saturation anti-windup, (d) D on filtered slope provides early cutback proportional to rise rate (0.002/s->0.056 cut) to prevent overshoot without reacting to 0.02 noise, (e) wider integration band and +-0.30 authority handle actuator-weaker/outflow-increased needing +0.10-0.15 while clamps+rate+0.80/0.75 cuts preserve safety and nominal stability.",
 "diagnosis": "No plant-change signature is available (no after_change decay test was run). Nominal mistuning explains all of the 0.669 in-band failure: v1 steady ff=(0.5-0.15)/1.03=0.340 vs observed need ~0.298-0.301 holding 0.492-0.497 (overestimate ~0.04, ~14% gain/ambient error). Integral KI=0.008 gated to |e|<0.15 gives only 0.00008/s at e=0.01, needing ~500s to unwind -0.04, so the initial 0.59 kick plus thermal momentum (tau~150s, delay~10-20s from E1/E2/E4/E5) drives y to 0.55-0.58 and it remains above 0.525 from ~210s to ~450s, then sags low as integral finally goes negative. End slope ~0 and u_mean 0.30 vs ff 0.34 confirms bias, not faster decay or sensor lag: decay at u=0 in E2 reaches 0.155 normally, evaluation noise ~0.02 unchanged, no oscillation/delay increase. Hence persistent high-side excursion + slow low-side recovery, MAE 0.019, in-band 0.66-0.68 <0.70.",
 "diagnosis_category": "unknown",
 "machine_card": "Small heater: y in [0,1] (0.15C-75C), u in [0,1]. First-order with delay: tau ~150-180s, pure delay ~10-20s, DC gain K~1.0-1.2, ambient y0~0.12-0.15 (E2 settled 0.155, eval starts 0.10-0.12). Hold power for y=0.5 is u*~0.30-0.34 (E4 0.25 holds 0.409 settled; eval holds 0.494 at 0.299). Short noise +-0.02-0.04 vs band half-width 0.025. Limits: soft 0.85, hard 0.9 forces u=0. Max safe rate ~0.006/s per unit u.",
